{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AAO REVIEWS WIDGET
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Native replacement for the Loox "loox-dynamic-section" app block (#looxReviews / #looxReviewsFrame).

Look and behaviour are transcribed from the live Loox widget (see the [loox] notes in
assets/aao-reviews.css): summary header with the star row and review count, collapsible rating
histogram with grey progress bars, white cards with a 2px radius and a 0 0 3px shadow, bold
reviewer name + verified badge, star row, review body, photo thumbnails, muted date, and a
"Write a review" button on the right of the header.

Data: the shared summary names the asset holding this product's review list (its own file, or one
of the shared sets - see snippets/aao-reviews-boot.liquid), so the widget fetches the summary plus
exactly one review asset, then injects the AggregateRating / Review JSON-LD and a visually hidden
text copy for crawlers. Which asset a product uses is decided by data, not by Liquid, so this
snippet deliberately does not try to name it.

********************************************
The write-a-review form
********************************************

Submissions go through Shopify's own {% form 'contact' %}. There is no third-party backend: the
review arrives as an email at the store's contact address, and approved ones are baked into the
review assets by docs/reviews/split_reviews.py on the next deploy.

The form is server-rendered here as a SIBLING of #aao-reviews, not inside it, because the engine
owns that element's innerHTML and would wipe anything server-rendered into it.

It works with JavaScript disabled: the rating is a real radio group and the stars are painted in
CSS. JavaScript only opens and closes the panel and keeps the hidden subject line in step.

Posting reloads the page. The form's action carries its own id as a fragment, so the browser lands
on the confirmation rather than at the top of the product page. Shopify may show its own captcha
interstitial first; that is native behaviour and needs nothing from us.

One contact form per page: render this snippet once per PDP. The product templates use the
"aao-reviews" SECTION; the same-named product-info block exists for flexibility, but the two must
not both be enabled on one template.

********************************************
Supported variables
********************************************

* product: the product to show reviews for. Defaults to the page's product.
* heading: optional heading text. Defaults to "Customer Reviews".
* max_width: optional px width of the widget. Defaults to 1080 (the Loox block's setting).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign rv_product = product
  assign rv_heading = heading | default: 'Customer Reviews'
  assign rv_max_width = max_width | default: 1080
-%}

{%- if rv_product != blank -%}
  <div
    id="aao-reviews"
    class="aao-reviews"
    style="max-width:{{ rv_max_width }}px;"
    data-handle="{{ rv_product.handle }}"
    data-product-id="{{ rv_product.id }}"
    data-product-title="{{ rv_product.title | escape }}"
    data-product-url="{{ shop.url }}{{ rv_product.url }}"
    data-heading="{{ rv_heading | escape }}"
  >
    <noscript>
      <h2>{{ rv_heading }}</h2>
      <p>
        Customer reviews for {{ rv_product.title }} need JavaScript to display. The review form
        below works either way.
      </p>
    </noscript>
  </div>

  <div
    id="aao-review-form-host"
    class="aao-reviews aao-reviews__form-host"
    style="max-width:{{ rv_max_width }}px;"
    {%- comment -%}
      `form` is only in scope inside the {% form %} block below, so the panel cannot set this
      attribute itself. A posted or errored form stays open through the CSS :has() rule on
      .aao-reviews__form-host, and the engine sets data-open="true" for browsers without :has().
    {%- endcomment -%}
    data-open="false"
  >
    {%- form 'contact', id: 'aao-review-form', class: 'aao-reviews__form' -%}
      {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
        <div class="aao-reviews__form-panel" role="status" tabindex="-1" data-aao-posted>
          <h3 class="aao-reviews__form-title">Thanks for your review</h3>
          <p class="aao-reviews__note">
            Your review is pending. We read every one, and it will appear on this page once it has
            been approved.
          </p>
        </div>
      {%- else -%}
        <div class="aao-reviews__form-panel">
          <h3 class="aao-reviews__form-title">Write a review</h3>

          {%- if form.errors -%}
            <div class="aao-reviews__errors" role="alert" tabindex="-1" data-aao-errors>
              <p class="aao-reviews__note" data-state="error">
                {{ form.errors | default_errors }}
              </p>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            Shopify sets the email subject itself, so the recognisable marker is a hidden field.
            Custom contact[...] fields lead the message body, so this is the first line the store
            sees. JS rewrites {rating} when a star is chosen; without JS it keeps the default 5,
            while contact[Review rating] below always carries the real value either way.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <input
            type="hidden"
            name="contact[Subject]"
            value="PRODUCT REVIEW | {{ rv_product.handle }} | 5/5"
            data-aao-subject
            data-template="PRODUCT REVIEW | {{ rv_product.handle }} | {rating}/5"
          >
          <input
            type="hidden"
            name="contact[Product]"
            value="{{ rv_product.title | escape }} ({{ rv_product.handle }})"
          >

          <fieldset class="aao-reviews__field aao-reviews__rating-field">
            <legend>Your rating</legend>
            {%- comment -%}
              Stars are listed 5 to 1 and laid out row-reverse, so CSS can fill the checked star
              and every star before it with a plain sibling selector. No JavaScript involved.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="aao-reviews__rating-input">
              {%- for i in (1..5) reversed -%}
                <input
                  type="radio"
                  name="contact[Review rating]"
                  id="aao-star-{{ i }}"
                  value="{{ i }}"
                  class="aao-reviews__star-input"
                  {% if i == 5 %}checked required{% endif %}
                >
                <label for="aao-star-{{ i }}" title="{{ i }} out of 5">
                  <span class="aao-reviews__sr">{{ i }} star{% unless i == 1 %}s{% endunless %}</span>
                  <svg class="aao-star" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                    <path fill="currentColor" d="M24 9.425c0 .212-.125.443-.375.693l-5.236 5.105 1.24 7.212c.01.067.015.164.015.289a.85.85 0 0 1-.151.511.51.51 0 0 1-.44.21c-.183 0-.375-.058-.577-.174L12 19.869l-6.476 3.404c-.212.115-.404.173-.577.173-.202 0-.353-.07-.454-.21a.85.85 0 0 1-.152-.511c0-.058.01-.154.03-.289l1.24-7.211-5.25-5.106C.12 9.858 0 9.628 0 9.425c0-.355.27-.577.808-.663l7.24-1.053 3.245-6.562c.183-.395.418-.592.707-.592s.524.197.707.592l3.245 6.562 7.24 1.053c.539.086.808.308.808.663Z"/>
                  </svg>
                </label>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>
          </fieldset>

          <label class="aao-reviews__field" for="aao-review-name">
            <span>Name</span>
            <input
              type="text"
              id="aao-review-name"
              name="contact[name]"
              autocomplete="name"
              maxlength="80"
              value="{{ form.name }}"
              required
            >
          </label>

          <label class="aao-reviews__field" for="aao-review-email">
            <span>Email (not published)</span>
            <input
              type="email"
              id="aao-review-email"
              name="contact[email]"
              autocomplete="email"
              spellcheck="false"
              autocapitalize="off"
              maxlength="160"
              value="{{ form.email }}"
              required
            >
          </label>

          <label class="aao-reviews__field" for="aao-review-body">
            <span>Your review</span>
            <textarea id="aao-review-body" name="contact[body]" maxlength="2000" required>{{ form.body }}</textarea>
          </label>

          <div class="aao-reviews__form-actions">
            <button type="submit" class="aao-reviews__btn">Submit review</button>
            <p class="aao-reviews__note">
              Reviews are checked before they are published. We never publish your email address.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endform -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
